lternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":161000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-54590/s66-54590~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-19225/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1965-03-23T00:00:00Z","description":"S65-19225 (23 March 1965) --- This view of astronauts John W. Young (left), pilot, and Virgil I. Grissom, command pilot, was taken through the window of the open hatch on Young's side of the Gemini-Titan 3 spacecraft just before the hatches were closed in readiness for their three-orbit flight.","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s65-19225","title":"JOHN W. YOUNG"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-19225/s65-19225~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1010,"size":109000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-19225/s65-19225~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":505,"size":36000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-19225/s65-19225~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":505,"size":36000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-19225/s65-19225~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1516,"size":231000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s65-19225/s65-19225~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54555/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-09-14T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-54555 (14 Sept. 1966) --- The Gemini-11 spacecraft is docked to the Agena Target Vehicle in this photograph taken by astronaut Richard F. Gordon Jr., pilot, as he stood in the open hatch of the Gemini-11 spacecraft during his extravehicular activity (EVA). Note Agena's L-band antenna. Taken during Gemini-11's 29th revolution of Earth, using a modified 70mm Hasselblad camera, with Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome, MS (S.O. 368) color film. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["AGENA ROCKET VEHICLES","EXTRAVEHICULAR ACTIVITY","HATCHES","PHOTOGRAPHS","TARGETS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-54555","title":"Docking - Gemini-Titan (GT)-11 - Outer Space"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54555/S66-54555~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":90000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54555/S66-54555~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":26000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54555/S66-54555~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":26000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54555/S66-54555~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":200000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-54555/S66-54555~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-01-15T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-18602 (16 March 1966) --- Astronauts Neil A. Armstrong and David R. Scott sit with their spacecraft hatches open while awaiting the arrival of the recovery ship, the USS Leonard F. Mason after the successful completion of their Gemini-8 mission. They are assisted by U.S. Navy divers. The overhead view shows the Gemini-8 spacecraft with the yellow flotation collar attached to stabilize the spacecraft in choppy seas. The green marker dye is highly visible from the air and is used as a locating aid. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-18602","title":"Gemini 8 Recovery - Astronaut David R. Scott - Miscellaneous - Atlantic"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":207000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":62000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":62000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":454000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-18602/s66-18602~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image","height":4536,"width":4536,"size":3800000}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-62926/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-12T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-62926 (12 Nov. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin Jr., pilot of the Gemini-12 spaceflight, is photographed with pilot's hatch of the spacecraft open. Note: J.A. Maurer camera which was used to photograph some of his extravehicular activity (EVA). Astronaut James A. Lovell Jr. was the command pilot. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 12 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","ASTRONAUTS"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"S66-62926","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - EARTH SKY - EXTRAVEHICULAR ACTIVITY (EVA) - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-62926/S66-62926~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":93000,"height":1272},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-62926/S66-62926~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":33000,"height":636},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-62926/S66-62926~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":33000,"height":636},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-62926/S66-62926~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":186000,"height":1908},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/S66-62926/S66-62926~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63537/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-11-11T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-63537 (11 Nov. 1966) --- Astronaut Edwin E. Aldrin, pilot for the Gemini-12 spaceflight, stands up in the open hatch of the spacecraft during the first day of the four-day mission in space. He prepares a camera for installation on the outside of the spacecraft. Command pilot for the last flight in the Gemini series was astronaut James A. Lovell Jr. Photo credit: NASA","media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-63537","title":"GEMINI-TITAN (GT)-12 - EARTH SKY - EXTRAVEHICULAR ACTIVITY (EVA) - OUTER SPACE"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63537/s66-63537~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":83000,"height":903},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63537/s66-63537~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":29000,"height":451},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63537/s66-63537~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":29000,"height":451},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63537/s66-63537~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":168000,"height":1355},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-63537/s66-63537~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38070/collection.json","data":[{"center":"JSC","date_created":"1966-06-05T00:00:00Z","description":"S66-38070 (5 June 1966) --- Northwestern Mexico as seen from the Gemini-9A spacecraft during its 32nd revolution of Earth. The large penisula is Baja California. The body of water at lower right is the Pacific Ocean. The land mass at upper left is the State of Sonora. The Gulf of California separates Sonora from the peninsula. The nose of the spacecraft is at left; and at right is the open hatch of the spacecraft. Astronaut Eugene A. Cernan, pilot, took this picture with his modified 70mm Hasselblad EVA camera, using Eastman Kodak, Ektachrome, MS (S.O. 217) color film. Photo credit: NASA","keywords":["GEMINI 9 FLIGHT","GEMINI PROJECT","EXTRAVEHICULAR ACTIVITY","EARTH OBSERVATIONS (FROM SPACE)"],"media_type":"image","nasa_id":"s66-38070","title":"GEMINI-9 - EARTH SKY - NORTHWESTERN MEXICO, BAJA CALIFORNIA"}],"links":[{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38070/s66-38070~medium.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1280,"size":110000,"height":1280},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38070/s66-38070~small.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":640,"size":36000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38070/s66-38070~thumb.jpg","rel":"preview","render":"image","width":640,"size":36000,"height":640},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38070/s66-38070~large.jpg","rel":"alternate","render":"image","width":1920,"size":247000,"height":1920},{"href":"https://images-assets.nasa.gov/image/s66-38070/s66-38070~orig.jpg","rel":"canonical","render":"image"}]}],"metadata":{"total_hits":12}}}